Q-5:-Compare your procedural C version and OOP TaskList version: List 3
 problems you faced in the C version that were solved by using classes
 and methods in the OOP version.
 
ANS:-
C Version
 In the procedural C version, managing tasks was a little difficult. We had to
 use arrays and separate functions to store and manage tasks. Marking a task 
 as done required extra handling, and as the number of tasks increased, the 
 code became more difficult to organize and maintain.

OOP Version

 In the OOP version, these problems were solved using classes and methods. The
 Task class stores the task details, while the TaskList class manages multiple
 tasks. Methods like addTask(), markTaskDone(), and showTasks() make the 
 program more organized, simple, and easy to manage.
